{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding where code runs is fundamental to building TanStack Start applications. This guide explains TanStack Start's execution model and how to control where your code executes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-principle-isomorphic-by-default","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core Principle: Isomorphic by Default"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All code in TanStack Start is isomorphic by default"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - it runs and is included in both server and client bundles unless explicitly constrained."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ✅ This runs on BOTH server and client\nfunction formatPrice(price: number) {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n    style: 'currency',\n    currency: 'USD',\n  }).format(price)\n}\n\n// ✅ Route loaders are ISOMORPHIC\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This runs on server during SSR AND on client during navigation\n    const response = await fetch('/api/products')\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Critical Understanding"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Route "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":"s are isomorphic - they run on both server and client, not just the server."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-execution-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Execution Boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start applications run in two environments:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server-environment","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Environment"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node.js runtime"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with access to file system, databases, environment variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Initial page renders on server"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API requests"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Server functions execute server-side"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build time"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Static generation and pre-rendering"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"client-environment","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Environment"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser runtime"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with access to DOM, localStorage, user interactions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Client takes over after initial server render"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Route loaders run client-side during navigation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User interactions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Event handlers, form submissions, etc."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"execution-control-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution Control APIs"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server-only-execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-Only Execution"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Case"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerFn()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RPC calls, data mutations"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Network request to server"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerOnlyFn(fn)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Utility functions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws error"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFn, createServerOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// RPC: Server execution, callable from client\nconst updateUser = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator((data: UserData) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    // Only runs on server, but client can call it\n    return await db.users.update(data)\n  })\n\n// Utility: Server-only, client crashes if called\nconst getEnvVar = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.DATABASE_URL)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"client-only-execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-Only Execution"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Case"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createClientOnlyFn(fn)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser utilities"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<ClientOnly>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components needing browser APIs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders fallback"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createClientOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { ClientOnly } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Utility: Client-only, server crashes if called\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((key: string, value: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value))\n})\n\n// Component: Only renders children after hydration\nfunction Analytics() {\n  return (\n    <ClientOnly fallback={null}>\n      <GoogleAnalyticsScript />\n    </ClientOnly>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"usehydrated-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHydrated Hook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more granular control over hydration-dependent behavior, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHydrated"},{"type":"text","value":" hook. It returns an accessor (signal) indicating whether the client has been hydrated:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useHydrated } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nfunction TimeZoneDisplay() {\n  const hydrated = useHydrated()\n  const timeZone = () =>\n    hydrated() ? Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone : 'UTC'\n\n  return <div>Your timezone: {timeZone()}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Always returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First client render"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" (and stays "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for all subsequent renders)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful when you need to conditionally render content based on client-side data (like browser timezone, locale, or localStorage) while providing a sensible fallback for server rendering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-specific-implementations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment-Specific Implementations"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createIsomorphicFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Different implementation per environment\nconst getDeviceInfo = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => ({ type: 'server', platform: process.platform }))\n  .client(() => ({ type: 'client', userAgent: navigator.userAgent }))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"architectural-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Architectural Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"progressive-enhancement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Progressive Enhancement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build components that work without JavaScript and enhance with client-side functionality:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-aware-storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment-Aware Storage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rpc-vs-direct-function-calls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RPC vs Direct Function Calls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding when to use server functions vs server-only functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// createServerFn: RPC pattern - server execution, client callable\nconst fetchUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => await db.users.find())\n\n// Usage from client component:\nconst user = await fetchUser() // ✅ Network request\n\n// createServerOnlyFn: Crashes if called from client\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET)\n\n// Usage from client:\nconst secret = getSecret() // ❌ Throws error","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-anti-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Anti-Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variable-exposure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable Exposure"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"incorrect-loader-assumptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incorrect Loader Assumptions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hydration-mismatches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration Mismatches"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-vs-api-driven-environment-detection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual vs API-Driven Environment Detection"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Manual: You handle the logic\nfunction logMessage(msg: string) {\n  if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n    console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`)\n  } else {\n    console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// API: Framework handles it\nconst logMessage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"architecture-decision-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Architecture Decision Framework"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose Server-Only when:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessing sensitive data (environment variables, secrets)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File system operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Database connections"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External API keys"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose Client-Only when:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM manipulation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser APIs (localStorage, geolocation)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User interaction handling"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Analytics/tracking"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose Isomorphic when:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data formatting/transformation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Business logic"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared utilities"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route loaders (they're isomorphic by nature)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"security-considerations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security Considerations"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"bundle-analysis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundle Analysis"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always verify server-only code isn't included in client bundles:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Analyze client bundle\nnpm run build\n# Check dist/client for any server-only imports","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variable-strategy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable Strategy"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-exposed"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VITE_"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix for client-accessible variables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-only"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Access via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerOnlyFn()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerFn()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never expose"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Database URLs, API keys, secrets"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error-boundaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Boundaries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle server/client execution errors gracefully:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ErrorBoundary(props) {\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundaryComponent\n      fallback={<div>Something went wrong</div>}\n      onError={(error) => {\n        if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n          console.error('[SERVER ERROR]:', error)\n        } else {\n          console.error('[CLIENT ERROR]:', error)\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {props.children}\n    </ErrorBoundaryComponent>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding TanStack Start's execution model is crucial for building secure, performant, and maintainable applications. The isomorphic-by-default approach provides flexibility while the execution control APIs give you precise control when needed."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"core-principle-isomorphic-by-default","text":"Core Principle: Isomorphic by Default","level":2},{"id":"the-execution-boundary","text":"The Execution Boundary","level":2},{"id":"server-environment","text":"Server Environment","level":3},{"id":"client-environment","text":"Client Environment","level":3},{"id":"execution-control-apis","text":"Execution Control APIs","level":2},{"id":"server-only-execution","text":"Server-Only Execution","level":3},{"id":"client-only-execution","text":"Client-Only Execution","level":3},{"id":"usehydrated-hook","text":"useHydrated Hook","level":4},{"id":"environment-specific-implementations","text":"Environment-Specific Implementations","level":3},{"id":"architectural-patterns","text":"Architectural Patterns","level":2},{"id":"progressive-enhancement","text":"Progressive Enhancement","level":3},{"id":"environment-aware-storage","text":"Environment-Aware Storage","level":3},{"id":"rpc-vs-direct-function-calls","text":"RPC vs Direct Function Calls","level":3},{"id":"common-anti-patterns","text":"Common Anti-Patterns","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-exposure","text":"Environment Variable Exposure","level":3},{"id":"incorrect-loader-assumptions","text":"Incorrect Loader Assumptions","level":3},{"id":"hydration-mismatches","text":"Hydration Mismatches","level":3},{"id":"manual-vs-api-driven-environment-detection","text":"Manual vs API-Driven Environment Detection","level":2},{"id":"architecture-decision-framework","text":"Architecture Decision Framework","level":2},{"id":"security-considerations","text":"Security Considerations","level":2},{"id":"bundle-analysis","text":"Bundle Analysis","level":3},{"id":"environment-variable-strategy","text":"Environment Variable Strategy","level":3},{"id":"error-boundaries","text":"Error Boundaries","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUnderstanding where code runs is fundamental to building TanStack Start applications. This guide explains TanStack Start's execution model and how to control where your code executes.\n\n## Core Principle: Isomorphic by Default\n\n**All code in TanStack Start is isomorphic by default** - it runs and is included in both server and client bundles unless explicitly constrained.\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ This runs on BOTH server and client\nfunction formatPrice(price: number) {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n    style: 'currency',\n    currency: 'USD',\n  }).format(price)\n}\n\n// ✅ Route loaders are ISOMORPHIC\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This runs on server during SSR AND on client during navigation\n    const response = await fetch('/api/products')\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> **Critical Understanding**: Route `loader`s are isomorphic - they run on both server and client, not just the server.\n\n## The Execution Boundary\n\nTanStack Start applications run in two environments:\n\n### Server Environment\n\n- **Node.js runtime** with access to file system, databases, environment variables\n- **During SSR** - Initial page renders on server\n- **API requests** - Server functions execute server-side\n- **Build time** - Static generation and pre-rendering\n\n### Client Environment\n\n- **Browser runtime** with access to DOM, localStorage, user interactions\n- **After hydration** - Client takes over after initial server render\n- **Navigation** - Route loaders run client-side during navigation\n- **User interactions** - Event handlers, form submissions, etc.\n\n## Execution Control APIs\n\n### Server-Only Execution\n\n| API                      | Use Case                  | Client Behavior           |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `createServerFn()`       | RPC calls, data mutations | Network request to server |\n| `createServerOnlyFn(fn)` | Utility functions         | Throws error              |\n\n```tsx\nimport { createServerFn, createServerOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// RPC: Server execution, callable from client\nconst updateUser = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator((data: UserData) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    // Only runs on server, but client can call it\n    return await db.users.update(data)\n  })\n\n// Utility: Server-only, client crashes if called\nconst getEnvVar = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.DATABASE_URL)\n```\n\n### Client-Only Execution\n\n| API                      | Use Case                        | Server Behavior  |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `createClientOnlyFn(fn)` | Browser utilities               | Throws error     |\n| `<ClientOnly>`           | Components needing browser APIs | Renders fallback |\n\n```tsx\nimport { createClientOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { ClientOnly } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Utility: Client-only, server crashes if called\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((key: string, value: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value))\n})\n\n// Component: Only renders children after hydration\nfunction Analytics() {\n  return (\n    <ClientOnly fallback={null}>\n      <GoogleAnalyticsScript />\n    </ClientOnly>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### useHydrated Hook\n\nFor more granular control over hydration-dependent behavior, use the `useHydrated` hook. It returns an accessor (signal) indicating whether the client has been hydrated:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHydrated } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nfunction TimeZoneDisplay() {\n  const hydrated = useHydrated()\n  const timeZone = () =>\n    hydrated() ? Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone : 'UTC'\n\n  return <div>Your timezone: {timeZone()}</div>\n}\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n- **During SSR**: Always returns `false`\n- **First client render**: Returns `false`\n- **After hydration**: Returns `true` (and stays `true` for all subsequent renders)\n\nThis is useful when you need to conditionally render content based on client-side data (like browser timezone, locale, or localStorage) while providing a sensible fallback for server rendering.\n\n### Environment-Specific Implementations\n\n```tsx\nimport { createIsomorphicFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Different implementation per environment\nconst getDeviceInfo = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => ({ type: 'server', platform: process.platform }))\n  .client(() => ({ type: 'client', userAgent: navigator.userAgent }))\n```\n\n## Architectural Patterns\n\n### Progressive Enhancement\n\nBuild components that work without JavaScript and enhance with client-side functionality:\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Environment-Aware Storage\n\n```tsx\nconst storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })\n```\n\n### RPC vs Direct Function Calls\n\nUnderstanding when to use server functions vs server-only functions:\n\n```tsx\n// createServerFn: RPC pattern - server execution, client callable\nconst fetchUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => await db.users.find())\n\n// Usage from client component:\nconst user = await fetchUser() // ✅ Network request\n\n// createServerOnlyFn: Crashes if called from client\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET)\n\n// Usage from client:\nconst secret = getSecret() // ❌ Throws error\n```\n\n## Common Anti-Patterns\n\n### Environment Variable Exposure\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)\n```\n\n### Incorrect Loader Assumptions\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})\n```\n\n### Hydration Mismatches\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Manual vs API-Driven Environment Detection\n\n```tsx\n// Manual: You handle the logic\nfunction logMessage(msg: string) {\n  if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n    console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`)\n  } else {\n    console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// API: Framework handles it\nconst logMessage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))\n```\n\n## Architecture Decision Framework\n\n**Choose Server-Only when:**\n\n- Accessing sensitive data (environment variables, secrets)\n- File system operations\n- Database connections\n- External API keys\n\n**Choose Client-Only when:**\n\n- DOM manipulation\n- Browser APIs (localStorage, geolocation)\n- User interaction handling\n- Analytics/tracking\n\n**Choose Isomorphic when:**\n\n- Data formatting/transformation\n- Business logic\n- Shared utilities\n- Route loaders (they're isomorphic by nature)\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n### Bundle Analysis\n\nAlways verify server-only code isn't included in client bundles:\n\n```bash\n# Analyze client bundle\nnpm run build\n# Check dist/client for any server-only imports\n```\n\n### Environment Variable Strategy\n\n- **Client-exposed**: Use `VITE_` prefix for client-accessible variables\n- **Server-only**: Access via `createServerOnlyFn()` or `createServerFn()`\n- **Never expose**: Database URLs, API keys, secrets\n\n### Error Boundaries\n\nHandle server/client execution errors gracefully:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ErrorBoundary(props) {\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundaryComponent\n      fallback={<div>Something went wrong</div>}\n      onError={(error) => {\n        if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n          console.error('[SERVER ERROR]:', error)\n        } else {\n          console.error('[CLIENT ERROR]:', error)\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {props.children}\n    </ErrorBoundaryComponent>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nUnderstanding TanStack Start's execution model is crucial for building secure, performant, and maintainable applications. The isomorphic-by-default approach provides flexibility while the execution control APIs give you precise control when needed.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: execution-model\ntitle: Execution Model\n---\n\nUnderstanding where code runs is fundamental to building TanStack Start applications. This guide explains TanStack Start's execution model and how to control where your code executes.\n\n## Core Principle: Isomorphic by Default\n\n**All code in TanStack Start is isomorphic by default** - it runs and is included in both server and client bundles unless explicitly constrained.\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ This runs on BOTH server and client\nfunction formatPrice(price: number) {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n    style: 'currency',\n    currency: 'USD',\n  }).format(price)\n}\n\n// ✅ Route loaders are ISOMORPHIC\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This runs on server during SSR AND on client during navigation\n    const response = await fetch('/api/products')\n    return response.json()\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> **Critical Understanding**: Route `loader`s are isomorphic - they run on both server and client, not just the server.\n\n## The Execution Boundary\n\nTanStack Start applications run in two environments:\n\n### Server Environment\n\n- **Node.js runtime** with access to file system, databases, environment variables\n- **During SSR** - Initial page renders on server\n- **API requests** - Server functions execute server-side\n- **Build time** - Static generation and pre-rendering\n\n### Client Environment\n\n- **Browser runtime** with access to DOM, localStorage, user interactions\n- **After hydration** - Client takes over after initial server render\n- **Navigation** - Route loaders run client-side during navigation\n- **User interactions** - Event handlers, form submissions, etc.\n\n## Execution Control APIs\n\n### Server-Only Execution\n\n| API                      | Use Case                  | Client Behavior           |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `createServerFn()`       | RPC calls, data mutations | Network request to server |\n| `createServerOnlyFn(fn)` | Utility functions         | Throws error              |\n\n```tsx\nimport { createServerFn, createServerOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// RPC: Server execution, callable from client\nconst updateUser = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator((data: UserData) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    // Only runs on server, but client can call it\n    return await db.users.update(data)\n  })\n\n// Utility: Server-only, client crashes if called\nconst getEnvVar = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.DATABASE_URL)\n```\n\n### Client-Only Execution\n\n| API                      | Use Case                        | Server Behavior  |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `createClientOnlyFn(fn)` | Browser utilities               | Throws error     |\n| `<ClientOnly>`           | Components needing browser APIs | Renders fallback |\n\n```tsx\nimport { createClientOnlyFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { ClientOnly } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\n// Utility: Client-only, server crashes if called\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((key: string, value: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value))\n})\n\n// Component: Only renders children after hydration\nfunction Analytics() {\n  return (\n    <ClientOnly fallback={null}>\n      <GoogleAnalyticsScript />\n    </ClientOnly>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### useHydrated Hook\n\nFor more granular control over hydration-dependent behavior, use the `useHydrated` hook. It returns an accessor (signal) indicating whether the client has been hydrated:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHydrated } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nfunction TimeZoneDisplay() {\n  const hydrated = useHydrated()\n  const timeZone = () =>\n    hydrated() ? Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone : 'UTC'\n\n  return <div>Your timezone: {timeZone()}</div>\n}\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n\n- **During SSR**: Always returns `false`\n- **First client render**: Returns `false`\n- **After hydration**: Returns `true` (and stays `true` for all subsequent renders)\n\nThis is useful when you need to conditionally render content based on client-side data (like browser timezone, locale, or localStorage) while providing a sensible fallback for server rendering.\n\n### Environment-Specific Implementations\n\n```tsx\nimport { createIsomorphicFn } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Different implementation per environment\nconst getDeviceInfo = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => ({ type: 'server', platform: process.platform }))\n  .client(() => ({ type: 'client', userAgent: navigator.userAgent }))\n```\n\n## Architectural Patterns\n\n### Progressive Enhancement\n\nBuild components that work without JavaScript and enhance with client-side functionality:\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Environment-Aware Storage\n\n```tsx\nconst storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })\n```\n\n### RPC vs Direct Function Calls\n\nUnderstanding when to use server functions vs server-only functions:\n\n```tsx\n// createServerFn: RPC pattern - server execution, client callable\nconst fetchUser = createServerFn().handler(async () => await db.users.find())\n\n// Usage from client component:\nconst user = await fetchUser() // ✅ Network request\n\n// createServerOnlyFn: Crashes if called from client\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET)\n\n// Usage from client:\nconst secret = getSecret() // ❌ Throws error\n```\n\n## Common Anti-Patterns\n\n### Environment Variable Exposure\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)\n```\n\n### Incorrect Loader Assumptions\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})\n```\n\n### Hydration Mismatches\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Manual vs API-Driven Environment Detection\n\n```tsx\n// Manual: You handle the logic\nfunction logMessage(msg: string) {\n  if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n    console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`)\n  } else {\n    console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// API: Framework handles it\nconst logMessage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))\n```\n\n## Architecture Decision Framework\n\n**Choose Server-Only when:**\n\n- Accessing sensitive data (environment variables, secrets)\n- File system operations\n- Database connections\n- External API keys\n\n**Choose Client-Only when:**\n\n- DOM manipulation\n- Browser APIs (localStorage, geolocation)\n- User interaction handling\n- Analytics/tracking\n\n**Choose Isomorphic when:**\n\n- Data formatting/transformation\n- Business logic\n- Shared utilities\n- Route loaders (they're isomorphic by nature)\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n### Bundle Analysis\n\nAlways verify server-only code isn't included in client bundles:\n\n```bash\n# Analyze client bundle\nnpm run build\n# Check dist/client for any server-only imports\n```\n\n### Environment Variable Strategy\n\n- **Client-exposed**: Use `VITE_` prefix for client-accessible variables\n- **Server-only**: Access via `createServerOnlyFn()` or `createServerFn()`\n- **Never expose**: Database URLs, API keys, secrets\n\n### Error Boundaries\n\nHandle server/client execution errors gracefully:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ErrorBoundary(props) {\n  return (\n    <ErrorBoundaryComponent\n      fallback={<div>Something went wrong</div>}\n      onError={(error) => {\n        if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\n          console.error('[SERVER ERROR]:', error)\n        } else {\n          console.error('[CLIENT ERROR]:', error)\n        }\n      }}\n    >\n      {props.children}\n    </ErrorBoundaryComponent>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nUnderstanding TanStack Start's execution model is crucial for building secure, performant, and maintainable applications. The isomorphic-by-default approach provides flexibility while the execution control APIs give you precise control when needed.\n"}
